  "interpretation": "D1-S3k is a zero-network structural and field-validity QA over the completed D1-S3j direct-S3 rasters. It scans all 568 snapshot tiles, verifies raster semantics, rasterizes all 128,636 frozen 2025 fields tile-by-tile, and reports per-field and per-analysis-cell VALID coverage. Source geometry must remain the exact frozen, valid 2025 file. If reprojection alone creates a numerically invalid polygon, a tightly bounded in-memory make-valid repair may be used only for QA rasterization; it is reported, area-bounded and never persisted or treated as a geometry update. The >=24 all-four-snapshot pixel metric is a pre-B2 coverage screen only; exact B2 erosion and candidate discovery remain for D2. PASS permits a separate D2 full-Skane model/fusion execution stage, with low-coverage fields still allowed to become UNCERTAIN."
